@tradition row-for-the-board
// Round 2: two rowers race for Commander Vance's name at the top of the gym's rowing board, two minutes each. Every 4 weeks from week 8 (Days 51, 79...).
// The rowers first (3-gym-4, -11, -12, anim row; RV18 S4), then the rest of the gym.
// Rules: FX24 (0.93.2, behind TRAD_0932_ON in section 13). Words: CS1 (plans/trad-0932-words.txt, claude/crew-stories-pitch 7b1e7300).
k: 1309
title: Row for the board
when: every 4 weeks tuesday week 4 from day 50
at: 19:00-19:45
min: 20
where: 3 room Gym: gym, ids ^3-gym-(4|11|12)$
where: 3 pool gym
hold: 1,2
who: lindqvist-isak always, santos-zofia always, vance 60%, gym-regular 45%, runner 35%, everyone 8%
host: lindqvist-isak
from: lindqvist-isak
invite: host=lindqvist-isak odds=25% line="Row for the board. Two minutes each. Vance's name comes down tonight."

== mail
- Row for the board tomorrow, {time}, in the gym. Two minutes on the rower each, the gym shouts the numbers. Commander Vance's name is at the top. For now.

== ask
- Row for the board in the gym. Isak says tonight's the night. He says it every time.   #funny
- Vance is still top of the rowing board. Isak's taking it personally.
- Coming to shout the numbers at the rowing? Bring a voice.

== here
- Pull! Pull! Thirty seconds!
- Four hundred metres! Keep going!
- Is Vance watching? He's watching.   #funny
- Breathe. Then row. Then breathe.

== thanks
- Two rowers chase the name at the top of the rowing board, two minutes each, while the gym shouts the numbers. Commander Vance watches from the treadmill.

== chatter
- Isak got within three metres of Vance's time. Three!
- Vance watched the whole rowing race and said nothing. Then he rowed. Then he left.   #funny
- The rowing board hasn't changed yet. It will. Isak swears it will.
